<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treniota</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1264">1264</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Treniota was a Lithuanian duke and nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> who led resistance to the Livonian Order in the 1260s and encouraged the uprisings that followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe">Battle of Durbe</a>. In 1263 he and Daumantas murdered Mindaugas, and Treniota seized power as grand duke. He was himself killed in 1264 by Mindaugas's former servants, and Mindaugas's son Vaišvilkas took the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treniota.jpg" alt="Treniota" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Guagnini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Traniata._%D0%A2%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%8F%D1%82%D0%B0_(A._Guagnini,_1611).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
